**Definition 1.3 (original task).** $Q$ is AIF Definition 2.6 as instantiated
by ARC Definition 11.1 and UAS Definition 1.4, using the actual installed
original entry relation. Experiments use original prescribed Supply or
Advance and the original finite semantic/audit protocols at their real
admission points. Finite adaptive branching uses only acquired public
information. Responses retain legality, actual labels, released finite
outputs and the complete original joint successor after each executed
action. The empty response contains only running/terminal type and the
actual terminal output.

An enabled noncanonical Supply can be task-undefined while its raw IN
executes. A disabled or unauthorized trial instead has defined unexecuted
`none` and no receipt. An executed refusal retains its actual work and
successor. Write $x\sim_Q y$ for equality of the entire partial response
maps, including their domains. No new entry, diagnostic, successor field
or posthalt experiment is added here. In particular $Q_G$ is not used as
a replacement for $Q$.

